# QA before commit and push

## A. Docs and rules — before every commit (required)

No commit with code/API/DB changes without aligned docs/rules.

| If diff touches… | Update / verify |
| ---------------- | --------------- |
| `internal/<feature>/`, handlers, service | `docs/features/<feature>.md` |
| `api/openapi.yaml`, Postman, apicheck | same feature doc; remove stale endpoints from docs |
| `db/migrations/`, `db/queries/` | feature doc tables; new capability → `docs/status.md` |
| New naming/process pattern | matching `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` |
| Docs/rules only | no conflict with code, OpenAPI, `db/schema.sql` |

Run `make docs-check` (links, sizes, migration version in docs).

**Actuality:** docs describe **now** only; delete stale text in the same commit. Canon: code + OpenAPI + schema.

**status.md:** each row = live feature; new done capability → add row if missing.

Docs-only commits: still check links, duplicates, contradictions.

**Pre-commit hook:** after `make install-hooks` (included in `make setup`), each `git commit` runs `make check`. Override smoke only: `PRE_COMMIT_CHECK_FLAGS=--no-smoke git commit …`.

## B. Technical QA — before push

Full run: `make check` or `./scripts/check.sh`. CI parity: `make check-ci`.

| Step | Command |
| ---- | ------- |
| Format | `gofmt` |
| Vet / lint | `go vet`, golangci-lint |
| Unit tests | `go test ./...` |
| Build | `go build ./...` |
| sqlc drift | `sqlc generate` + clean `git diff internal/db/sqlc/` |
| go generate | `go generate ./internal/db/...` + diff |
| Contract | `SKIP_SMOKE=1 ./postman/validate.sh` |
| Migrate (full local) | `./scripts/migrate-check.sh` |
| Integration | `go test -tags integration ./internal/db/storetest/...` |
| Coverage | `./scripts/coverage.sh --min 85` |
| Smoke (full, API up) | `./postman/validate.sh` |
| After migrations | `make schema-sync` |

See [scripts/check.sh](../../scripts/check.sh) for flags (`--no-smoke`, etc.).
